          "filename": "26.05.84 Pwllheli Class 108 (6023810414).jpg",
          "caption": "Built by British Rail in Derby, 333 class 108 cars were built and operated in 2, 3 and 4 car sets. Seen at Pwhelli on 26 May 1984 is a 2-car and 3-car set coupled together for increased loadings on the Cambrian Coast on Saturdays during the summer season. The train was to form the 10:15 departure.",
